Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.31,0:00:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,YORD 관심, าง Evans
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.61,0:00:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,ARKOP Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.21,0:00:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Yucking to Jean!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.11,0:00:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.23,0:00:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,YuYi-S-Ti!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.43,0:00:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.35,0:00:27.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yuiki-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.71,0:00:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.11,0:01:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't look good, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.13,0:01:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time for me to do what\Nmy associates couldn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.29,0:01:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Defeat you two so we can all escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You couldn't begin to imagine what\Nmonster lurks in my deck. Tell me!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.59,0:01:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you'll find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.17,0:01:17.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm about to summon it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.77,0:01:23.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to my altar of mist, I can add\Nany ritual magic card I want in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.17,0:01:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.33,0:01:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Dragon Revival Ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.97,0:01:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This card allows me to summon my\Nall-powerful five-headed dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.71,0:01:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.93,0:01:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Very perceptive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.53,0:01:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I must also have five monsters,\Neach with a different attribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.25,0:01:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I may be missing something, but\NI only see one monster on your side.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.33,0:01:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.24,0:01:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You are missing something, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.97,0:01:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.88,0:01:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Jinzo isn't my only\NDeathmaster, remember? Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.69,0:01:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And what do you mean by that, Lecter?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.31,0:01:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, the other members are\Nthe big five. That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.33,0:01:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Their monsters count, too,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.97,0:02:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,because all five of those\Ncreeps are using Tristan's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.21,0:02:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And each one of them has\Ntheir own Deckmaster, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.33,0:02:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but that doesn't seem fair at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.79,0:02:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, these guys will do anything to win.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.69,0:02:11.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Who said they were fair?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.43,0:02:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,My five Deckmasters, come forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.01,0:02:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll call you all to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.97,0:02:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,First, the unstoppable gym zone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.25,0:02:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I summon the\Nalmighty Deep-Sea Warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.69,0:02:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Followed by the cunning\NNightmare Penguin Next,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.39,0:02:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll call Judge Man to\Nthe stand. And finally,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.01,0:02:35.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll summon the superior Robotic\NKnight. Now listen to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.61,0:02:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,my five Deck Masters I command\Nall of you to join together To
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.79,0:02:44.41,Default,,0,0,0,,form a creature of unparalleled\Nstrength and supreme power Behold,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.67,0:02:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,the ultimate monster My five-headed dragon
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.83,0:03:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,We faced this beast before. I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.89,0:03:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I forget?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.17,0:03:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the last time we\Nfought these cyber creeps.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.99,0:03:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That super dragon took out\Nmy monster, and me with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.97,0:03:12.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.37,0:03:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.75,0:03:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't leave us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.19,0:03:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,We've lost him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.15,0:03:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.06,0:03:20.11,Default,,0,0,0,,He's left us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.43,0:03:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's just hope my luck is\Nbetter than it was last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.41,0:03:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the good news is Lecter's dragon\Ncan't attack until his next turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.43,0:03:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.34,0:03:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.27,0:03:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,We have one turn to stop it. Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.69,0:03:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I forgot to mention.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.95,0:03:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,My dragon destroys\Nevery one of your magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.97,0:03:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,trap and monster cards\Nas soon as it's summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.35,0:03:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.81,0:03:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, Lector, we got plenty of monsters\Nin our decks, and it's our move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.61,0:03:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,There's one more thing you should know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.73,0:03:55.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It's immune to almost all attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.57,0:04:00.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It cannot be damaged by fire,\Nwater, earth, wind, or darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.01,0:04:01.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.23,0:04:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That leaves only one type of\Nmonster, creatures of light.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.95,0:04:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems to me that your chances of\Nrescuing Tristan just got even slimmer,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.41,0:04:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And I think you all know what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.25,0:04:16.57,Default,,0,0,0,,It means four more of\Nyou will soon join him as
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.65,0:04:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,part of the Big Five's\Nnewest corporate takeover.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.97,0:04:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And just to make sure no one interferes\Nwith our plan, I place this card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.61,0:04:25.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.17,0:04:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Now use your last turn wisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.65,0:04:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.53,0:04:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's got 5,000 attack points, and\Nonly one kind of monster can beat it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.13,0:04:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Any ideas, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.59,0:04:38.11,Default,,0,0,0,,We can do this, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.61,0:04:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust your Deckmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.73,0:04:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, my deck master.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.07,0:04:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,My flamed swordsman stood by me in my\Nlast duel and guided me to victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.61,0:04:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.09,0:04:48.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.17,0:04:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I was hoping for a monster card.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.47,0:04:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, you'll never\Nget me and my friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.25,0:04:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Got that, Lecter?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.39,0:05:00.86,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll place these three\Ncards face down on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.25,0:05:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Swordsman, it's all you out there now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.03,0:05:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I call my deck master to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.79,0:05:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,all right it's risky but i know we can do\Nthis together that's all for me good work
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.79,0:05:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,joey i know what i have to do i just hope
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.17,0:05:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,it works it's my move here goes i may need
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.95,0:05:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,this in a little while now i call my deck
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.07,0:05:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,master to the field\Ndark magician whoa yuki
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.27,0:05:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,and joey both called their deck masters\Nto the field isn't that dangerous if those
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.69,0:05:41.81,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters are destroyed they lose yeah but\Nsince they have no other monsters on the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.89,0:05:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,field that five-headed freak would have\Nsmashed them to smithereens anyway you've
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.83,0:05:53.73,Default,,0,0,0,,made this too easy your deck masters can't\Ntouch my dragon and the best part is once
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.81,0:06:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,i destroy them you two lose and your bodies\Nare ours hang in there i'm here for you
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.07,0:06:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel's not over,\NLecter, and it's our move.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.27,0:06:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll show you what real teamwork can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.09,0:06:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Very touchy, but I'd say five\Nheads are much better than two!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.55,0:06:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you plan to defeat our dragon?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.49,0:06:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The same way I did the\Nfirst time we fought it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.83,0:06:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.03,0:06:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That won't work now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.49,0:06:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Last time you summoned\NMaster of Dragon Soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.49,0:06:35.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's true, you can't\Nplay Master of Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.61,0:06:39.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have the cards you\Nneed to summon it to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.27,0:06:41.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.18,0:06:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,but I can summon a monster that's\Njust as powerful by combining
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.33,0:06:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,our two Deck Masters together in\Norder to form Dark Flare Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.83,0:06:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a good look, Big Five.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.43,0:07:04.39,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the monster that will bring about\Nyour destruction and return Tristan to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.53,0:07:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You challenge our dragon with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.53,0:07:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Dark Flare Knight is a\Ncombination of our Deckmasters.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.57,0:07:13.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as your dragon is\Na combination of yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.67,0:07:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And Joey and I have\Nfaith in our Deckmasters.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.25,0:07:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You fool, that new monster of\Nyours is a creature of darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.57,0:07:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And our five-headed dragon can only be\Nbeaten by a creature of light. We'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.11,0:07:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.02,0:07:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, we will.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.93,0:07:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's monster is so much\Nweaker than their dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.13,0:07:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,If he attacks, it's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.11,0:07:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, it's their deckmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.61,0:07:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,So if it's destroyed, they\Nlose the duel. Oh, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.35,0:07:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope Yugi knows what\Nhe's doing out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.69,0:07:42.40,Default,,0,0,0,,This move is our last chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.77,0:07:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Flare Knight, prepare to attack now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.15,0:07:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your target is their five-headed dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.49,0:07:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Take him down, my beast.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.53,0:08:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.65,0:08:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How can you two still be standing?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.19,0:08:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,We're unharmed because of Dark\NFlare Knight's special effects.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.23,0:08:17.59,Default,,0,0,0,,First, it prevents me from losing\Nlife points when it's destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.67,0:08:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's not all it does, Lector.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.21,0:08:21.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Our deckmasters are gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.09,0:08:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,But notice that Joey and I\Nare still in this duel. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.03,0:08:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid so.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.81,0:08:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Dark Flare\NKnight's second effect,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.65,0:08:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,whenever that card's destroyed, Mirage\NKnight is then summoned to take its place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.97,0:08:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's your new Death Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.23,0:08:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice try, Yugi, but this\Nknight's too weak, also.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.99,0:08:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,So why did you go through all this\Ntrouble just to bring that to the field?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.63,0:08:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless Mirage Knight has\Na special effect as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.83,0:08:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're beginning to catch on, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.51,0:08:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Mirage Knight, attack his dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.67,0:09:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,He may look weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.49,0:09:11.61,Default,,0,0,0,,However, first impressions\Ncan be deceiving.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.59,0:09:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,So observe closely now, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.57,0:09:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The special ability of our Mirage\NKnight is about to seal our victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.75,0:09:24.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, it is able to absorb all of the\Nattack points of the opposing monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.83,0:09:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Giving our monster 5,000\Nextra attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.31,0:09:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.01,0:09:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's more powerful than our dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.43,0:09:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And there's one more thing\Nyou may want to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.47,0:09:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Mirage Knight is a creature of light,\Nand you know what that means, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.79,0:09:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It's exactly the kind of monster\NI need to destroy your dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.95,0:09:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And once it's wiped out, this\Nduel will finally be over!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.47,0:09:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Deckmaster is now gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.05,0:10:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And since my Mirage Knight had 7,800\Nattack points, your life points are gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.21,0:10:08.29,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel's done! That's funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.57,0:10:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't feel like a loser.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.39,0:10:12.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.49,0:10:14.89,Default,,0,0,0,,His life points didn't drop to zero!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.33,0:10:17.43,Default,,0,0,0,,That attack should have wiped him out!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.51,0:10:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Explain yourself, tough guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.83,0:10:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you forget about the\Nface-down card I played earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.07,0:10:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It's known as a deal\Nwith Dark Ruler. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.39,0:10:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I should have known.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.55,0:10:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.53,0:10:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,this trap card prevented\Nme from receiving any
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.11,0:10:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,damage when your knight\Ndestroyed my dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.05,0:10:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All I had to do was give\Nup half of my life points,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.53,0:10:48.63,Default,,0,0,0,,a business decision that was\Nwell worth it in the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.71,0:10:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Wouldn't you agree?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.85,0:10:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,But you should still lose,\Nbecause your deck master's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.83,0:10:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That would've been the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.61,0:11:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,had it not been for the second effect\Nof my Dark Ruler Trap Card, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.79,0:11:01.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.65,0:11:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It summons Berserk Dragon\Nas my Death Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.23,0:11:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like your big plan did work, boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.25,0:11:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.16,0:11:18.66,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to our Mirage Knight?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.75,0:11:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gone now!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.66,0:11:23.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Mirage Knight only stays in\Nplay for one attack, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.67,0:11:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Then it splits into the two original monsters\Nthat were used to summon it. Oh, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.95,0:11:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now there's no way they can\Nstop the Big Five's dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.93,0:11:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Because that oversized freak show is way\Nstronger than either of their Deckmasters.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.17,0:11:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And when their Deckmasters go, so do they!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.65,0:11:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.33,0:11:42.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't let them\Ndestroy your Deckmasters!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.99,0:11:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about a thing, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.97,0:11:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Because Yugi's turn's not over yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.39,0:11:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You can do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.71,0:11:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.37,0:11:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate Magical Hats, so you'll\Nhave to find my Deckmaster to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.87,0:12:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And next, I shall activate my\NDeckmaster's special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.13,0:12:03.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll spend 1,000 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.49,0:12:05.73,Default,,0,0,0,,which allows my Dark Magician to duplicate
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.81,0:12:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,the effect of any magic card on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.43,0:12:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose Magical Hats, which\Nhides Joey's Deckmaster as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.63,0:12:15.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Hugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.71,0:12:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's hope these geezers\Naren't good at hide-and-seek.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.93,0:12:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.19,0:12:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The rest is up to fate, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.65,0:12:23.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's hope for the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.37,0:12:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not too worried.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.91,0:12:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He's got a one-in-four chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.67,0:12:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I have to disagree, Mr. Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.53,0:12:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Your math's a bit off.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.59,0:12:36.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The odds are slightly more in my favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.51,0:12:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And now it's time! My move!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.49,0:12:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll save this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.09,0:12:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, where were we?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.69,0:12:44.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yes, your little hat trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.83,0:12:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,A nice attempt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.91,0:12:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But since my new dragon can attack\Nfour monsters at the same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.15,0:12:51.39,Default,,0,0,0,,your hats won't work.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.09,0:12:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.00,0:12:54.05,Default,,0,0,0,,That means he can't miss.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.27,0:12:55.95,Default,,0,0,0,,One of us is about to lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.69,0:13:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So Yugi hit each monster in four hats, and\Nthis dragon can attack four hats at once?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.71,0:13:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.23,0:13:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy is making sure\Nhe hits his target.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.47,0:13:09.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So this is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.89,0:13:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid so.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.59,0:13:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,One of us is about to lose his Deckmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.83,0:13:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.74,0:13:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.95,0:13:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe Joey's got an idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.25,0:13:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe he's just lost his mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.53,0:13:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to lose it all, Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.63,0:13:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.71,0:13:31.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I'll target Yugi first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.15,0:13:34.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack, berserk dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.23,0:13:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's impolite to wear hats\Nin a place of business.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.41,0:13:43.01,Default,,0,0,0,,So destroy all four of Yugi's\Nhats, along with his deckmaster!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.55,0:13:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I tried my best, Tristan!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.77,0:13:48.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't give up, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.87,0:13:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my turn to save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.91,0:13:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Flame Swordsman, protect\NYugi with your life! No!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.91,0:13:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing, Joey?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.03,0:14:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,If his Death Master's\Ndestroyed, he loses! Stop, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.81,0:14:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Now both of your Death\NMasters are gone! No!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.51,0:14:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I win the duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.21,0:14:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You there, Joey?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.03,0:14:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Joey! He's okay! But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.85,0:14:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The dark magician survived!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.09,0:14:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And so did the flame swordsman!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.33,0:14:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheaters!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.24,0:14:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,How can your deckmasters be standing?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.07,0:14:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a look, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.55,0:14:41.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I used my trusty silver dollar trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.47,0:14:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Explain yourself! All right. First,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.55,0:14:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I saved Yu-Gi's Dark\NMagician by forcing my
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.95,0:14:49.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Flamed Swordsman to take\Nthe brunt of your attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.65,0:14:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, my Trap Card kicked\Nin and saved my Swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.77,0:14:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That card only saves weak monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.61,0:14:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.67,0:14:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey weakened his\NSwordsman when he used its
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.99,0:15:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,special ability to power\Nup his Rocket Warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.85,0:15:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So when Lecter's Dragon attacked,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.07,0:15:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's Silver Dollar Trap Card\Nsaved his already weak Swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.53,0:15:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,That was an excellent move, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.63,0:15:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, you managed to save us both.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.79,0:15:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you'd have done the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.97,0:15:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,So, what do you think about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.33,0:15:23.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, kid, I'm not through\Nwith you by a long shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.19,0:15:26.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And neither is my dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.81,0:15:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,So prepare to lose your bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.73,0:15:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,My dragon gets weaker with every turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.25,0:15:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, did you see that? You bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.11,0:15:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,His dragon just lost the dag points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.11,0:15:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Just in time for my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.09,0:15:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Check out this move, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.37,0:15:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Reveal my face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.57,0:15:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Knight's title.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.97,0:15:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll add this magic\Ncard to Yugi's Deckmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.35,0:16:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It transforms Dark Magician\Ninto Dark Magician Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.43,0:16:09.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, thanks to my\NDeckmaster's special power,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.43,0:16:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I can transfer most of its\Nattack points to Yu-Gi's.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.45,0:16:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Since this power only works on warriors,\NI had to transform Dark Magician first.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.33,0:16:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,3,200 attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.67,0:16:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That makes it stronger\Nthan my Berserk Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.01,0:16:26.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That should do the trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.63,0:16:28.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Now why don't you do the honors, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.97,0:16:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,With pleasure, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.99,0:16:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.53,0:16:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We make a great team, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.73,0:16:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Together, you and I are\Nabout to topple the Big Five.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.53,0:16:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I demand an explanation, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.17,0:16:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You said Wheeler would hold Yugi back.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.69,0:16:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, he's the reason\Nwhy they're ahead of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.35,0:16:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, don't look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.89,0:16:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You five are done.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.25,0:16:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My move.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.87,0:16:52.70,Default,,0,0,0,,And now,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.91,0:16:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Magician Knight attack their berserk\Ndragon with Sword of Dark Magic attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.63,0:17:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Carrying with him the combined\Nstrength of both of our deckmasters,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.53,0:17:06.24,Default,,0,0,0,,our knight cannot be stopped!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.41,0:17:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,There goes your Deckmaster. That means all
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.79,0:17:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,five of you automatically\Nlose this duel Now
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.21,0:17:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Return Tristan's body as you promised. And
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.23,0:17:29.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Run back to Noah. We've\Nall had enough of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.65,0:17:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a pleasure doing business\Nwith you gentlemen Yugi and
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.35,0:17:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey crushed those five creeps I\Nknew they would Way to go, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.41,0:17:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Tristan, I guess your days\Nof looking like a chimp are over.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.19,0:17:45.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, too bad I can't say\Nthe same for you, Duke.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.77,0:17:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now it's time for you five\Nto give Tristan his body back.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.51,0:17:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you've mistaken me for someone\Nwho believes in playing fair. Say, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.83,0:18:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, it's go time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.69,0:18:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.73,0:18:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Now to take five more bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.13,0:18:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.17,0:18:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Breaking my rules again, are we? Noah!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.91,0:18:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You five fools have failed\Nme for the last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.13,0:18:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What's happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.95,0:18:27.19,Default,,0,0,0,,They disappeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.93,0:18:28.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.93,0:18:31.28,Default,,0,0,0,,They took Tristan's body away with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.85,0:18:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.17,0:18:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be stuck in this monkey\Nsuit for the rest of my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.91,0:18:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm feeling more like a monkey and\Nless like me every second. This stinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.29,0:18:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm here for you, Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.87,0:18:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Second thought, I can\Nlearn to live with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.03,0:18:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.41,0:18:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The five of you are pathetic.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.25,0:19:00.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, Mokuba?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.23,0:19:04.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I hired you to defeat\NSeto and his friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.13,0:19:05.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Give us another chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.11,0:19:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll put them out of business.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.09,0:19:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Too late for that, Gansley.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.29,0:19:11.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Noah, help us.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.25,0:19:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We need these bodies to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.67,0:19:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been stuck in this virtual\Nabyss for what seems like forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.91,0:19:20.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You can save us.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.37,0:19:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Give us those bodies and we'll\Nhelp you take over, Kaivakor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.57,0:19:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.87,0:19:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd be better off with five\Nbaboons than you fools.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.93,0:19:33.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time for you to leave for good.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.21,0:19:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that clear?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.19,0:19:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave for good?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.61,0:19:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Please reconsider, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.39,0:19:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,As my father would say,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.13,0:19:43.51,Default,,0,0,0,,your work is unacceptable and\Ntherefore you must be eliminated now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.09,0:19:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I'll imprison each of you in a\Ndifferent corner of my work. Forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.77,0:19:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.99,0:19:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's time I challenge Seto personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.91,0:20:03.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll prove once and for all that I'm\Nthe true heir to the Kaiba Empire!
